# Rust workflow

ShellZip is a Cargo workspace: `crates/shellzip-core` (library), `crates/shellzip-cli` (bin `szip`), `crates/shellzip-gui` (bin `shellzip`). Edition 2024, stable toolchain pinned in `rust-toolchain.toml`, `unsafe_code = "forbid"` and `clippy::all = warn` at the workspace level.

## Before finishing any Rust change

Run the same gate as CI (`make ci` runs all three):

```
cargo fmt --all
cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo test --workspace
```

- Warnings are errors. Fix the cause; `#[allow(...)]` needs a same-line comment saying why.
- Iterate on one crate with `-p shellzip-core`, finish with `--workspace`.
- Before committing to `master`, also apply `cross-platform-release`: Windows-only helpers need `#[cfg(windows)]`, and non-Windows stubs must not use needless `return` (Linux clippy fails otherwise).

## Dependencies

- Add with `cargo add <crate> -p <member>`; use `default-features = false` and list only the features you use.
- Never hand-edit `Cargo.lock`; always commit it.
- Only MIT / Apache-2.0 / BSD-compatible licenses. Say what a new dependency replaces in the commit message.

## Skills in `.cursor/skills/`

`rust-quality-gate` (fmt/clippy/test loop), `rust-code-review`, `rust-testing`, `rust-scaffold` (new crate/module/command/bench), `rust-performance` (benchmark/profile/size).
